From: SpeedBreaker Project <speedbreaker-project@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 19:11:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Switch tables: index with the low 32 bits

A bounds-checked jump table compares the index with cmplwi and loads the
entry with rlwinm/lwzx, both 32-bit. 64-bit arithmetic before them (e.g.
addis) can leave carries in the upper half, so switching on the full
64-bit register can miss every case and hit __builtin_unreachable.
Seen in NFS: Most Wanted's sub_8217F390 (addis r11,r11,32764).
---
 XenonRecomp/recompiler.cpp | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/XenonRecomp/recompiler.cpp b/XenonRecomp/recompiler.cpp
index 5d822b1..9835368 100644
--- a/XenonRecomp/recompiler.cpp
+++ b/XenonRecomp/recompiler.cpp
@@ -609,7 +609,9 @@ bool Recompiler::Recompile(
     case PPC_INST_BCTR:
         if (switchTable != config.switchTables.end())
         {
-            println("\tswitch ({}.u64) {{", r(switchTable->second.r));
+            // The table index is the low word: 64-bit adds on the way (addis)
+            // can leave carries in the upper half that the hardware ignores.
+            println("\tswitch ({}.u32) {{", r(switchTable->second.r));
 
             for (size_t i = 0; i < switchTable->second.labels.size(); i++)
             {
